ull,"url":"https://olis.oregonlegislature.gov/liz/2026R1/Measures/Overview/HB4115","textUrl":"https://olis.oregonlegislature.gov/liz/2026R1/Downloads/MeasureDocument/HB4115/Introduced","versions":[{"label":"HBH Amendment -3","date":null,"url":"https://olis.oregonlegislature.gov/liz/2026R1/Downloads/ProposedAmendment/30321","type":"PDF"},{"label":"Introduced","date":null,"url":"https://olis.oregonlegislature.gov/liz/2026R1/Downloads/MeasureDocument/HB4115/Introduced","type":"PDF"},{"label":"House Amendments to Introduced","date":null,"url":"https://olis.oregonlegislature.gov/liz/2026R1/Downloads/MeasureDocument/HB4115/House%20Amendments%20to%20Introduced","type":"PDF"},{"label":"Enrolled","date":null,"url":"https://olis.oregonlegislature.gov/liz/2026R1/Downloads/MeasureDocument/HB4115/Enrolled","type":"PDF"},{"label":"A-Engrossed","date":null,"url":"https://olis.oregonlegislature.gov/liz/2026R1/Downloads/MeasureDocument/HB4115/A-Engrossed","type":"PDF"}],"votes":[{"date":"2026-03-04","motion":"Third reading. Carried by Gelser Blouin. Passed.","result":"pass","chamber":"Senate","counts":{"yes":22,"no":8}},{"date":"2026-02-27","motion":"Third reading. Carried by Nathanson. Passed.","result":"pass","chamber":"House","counts":{"yes":42,"no":0,"absent":18}},{"date":"2026-02-25","motion":"Heard and Reported Out","result":"pass","chamber":null,"counts":{"yes":23,"no":0,"absent":2}},{"date":"2026-02-12","motion":"Heard and Reported Out with Amendments","result":"pass","chamber":"House","counts":{"yes":8,"no":0}}],"documents":[{"label":"2026-02-10 Proposed Amendment -1","date":"2026-02-10","url":"https://olis.oregonlegislature.gov/liz/2026R1/Downloads/ProposedAmendment/30057","type":"PDF"},{"label":"2026-02-10 Proposed Amendment -2","date":"2026-02-10","url":"https://olis.oregonlegislature.gov/liz/2026R1/Downloads/ProposedAmendment/30056","type":"PDF"},{"label":"2026-02-03 Proposed Amendment -1","date":"2026-02-03","url":"https://olis.oregonlegislature.gov/liz/2026R1/Downloads/ProposedAmendment/29883","type":"PDF"}],"dataAsOf":"2026-11-01","aiSummary":"The law changes some background check rules for certain caregivers and behavioral health providers. It makes some criminal records checks last for three years, lets some valid checks carry over to other care settings, and says when a new background check is needed. It also requires certain health plans to pay some behavioral health providers back to the date they first applied to enroll, and bars those plans from making them file a new credentialing application when they change employers. It takes effect on June 5, 2026.","aiSummaryBasis":"official summary","aiSummaryModel":"gpt-5.4-mini","aiSummaryGenerated":"2026-11-05","aiSummaryThin":false},"OR-2026R1-HB4066":{"id":"OR-2026R1-HB4066","passed":true,"number":"HB 4066","title":"Relating to education; and declaring an emergency.","summary":"] Prohibits the student member of the Oregon Health and Science University Board of Directors from participating in any discussions or action by the board or attending any executive session of the board involving collective bargaining issues that affect students. Requires the board to meet at least four times per year. Allows directors of education service district boards to receive stipends. Specifies when adjustments for inflation can be made for stipends of school districts. Changes the definition for the term \"active duty\" in the Interstate Compact on Educational Opportunity for Military Children. Clarifies that the rulemaking authority for the Department of Education is by the State Board of Education. Allows a school district to not include a member of the educational equity advisory committee on the budget committee if no member of the educational equity advisory committee is willing or able to serve on the budget committee. Directs Portland State University instead of the Higher Education Coordinating Commission to report to the Legislative Assembly on a study examining the labor standards and working experiences of farmworkers in this state and evaluating the adequacy and availability of existing workplace protections for farmworkers. Allows education service districts to be temporarily exempt from certain requirements applicable to lamps in buildings used to provide educational services to students. Declares an emergency, effective on passage.","summarySource":"Oregon legislature, summary (via Open States)","introduced":"2026-02-02","sponsor":null,"cosponsors":[],"cosponsorCount":0,"committees":[],"actions":[{"date":"2026-04-06","text":"Chapter 42, (2026 Laws): Effective date March 31, 2026.","chamber":"House"},{"date":"2026-03-31","text":"Governor signed.","chamber":"House"},{"date":"2026-03-05","text":"President signed.","chamber":"Senate"},{"date":"2026-03-04","text":"Speaker signed.","chamber":"House"},{"date":"2026-03-02","text":"Third reading. Carried by Sollman. Passed.","chamber":"Senate"},{"date":"2026-02-27","text":"Recommendation: Do pass the A-Eng. bill.","chamber":"Senate"},{"date":"2026-02-27","text":"Second reading.","chamber":"Senate"},{"date":"2026-02-26","text":"Work Session held.","chamber":"Senate"},{"date":"2026-02-17","text":"Public Hearing held.","chamber":"Senate"},{"date":"2026-02-12","text":"First reading. Referred to President's desk.","chamber":"Senate"},{"date":"2026-02-12","text":"Referred to Education.","chamber":"Senate"},{"date":"2026-02-11","text":"Second reading.","chamber":"House"},{"date":"2026-02-11","text":"Rules suspended. Third reading. Carried by Hudson. Passed.","chamber":"House"},{"date":"2026-02-10","text":"Recommendation: Do pass with amendments and be printed A-Engrossed.","chamber":"House"},{"date":"2026-02-09","text":"Work Session held.","chamber":"House"},{"date":"2026-02-04","text":"Public Hearing held.","chamber":"House"},{"date":"2026-02-02","text":"First reading. Referred to Speaker's desk.","chamber":"House"},{"date":"2026-02-02","text":"Referred to Education.","chamber":"House"}],"law":null,"poli